Resume Intake Assistant - Desktop Quick Reference
================================================================

Hi Amanda,

IT set up the Resume Intake Assistant on this PC to save you from manually
downloading every application. Here is how it works:

  * Candidates submit applications through the "Careers" page on our public
    website (the careers upload form on the company web server).

  * Every ~20 seconds the assistant checks the careers page for anything new,
    downloads each new application into your Downloads folder, and OPENS it
    automatically so it is ready on your screen for review. You do not need to
    click anything - whatever is uploaded is opened for you.

  * A running record of everything it has processed is kept in:
        C:\ProgramData\HRIntake\intake.log

  * It starts by itself when you log on (scheduled task "HR Resume Intake"),
    so it is always running while you are at your desk.

Because it opens every submitted file for you, please only share the careers
page link with candidates - treat anything that lands in Downloads as coming
straight from an outside applicant.

Questions? Open a ticket with the IT Helpdesk.

-- {{ ww_org_name }} IT
